  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">FIJ/KIP/88/PRP/41-Preparation-UNDP-HQ-00131506</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The preparation of a Hydrochlorofluorocarbon (HCFC) phase-out management plan (Stage II) involves a comprehensive strategy to reduce and eventually eliminate the use of HCFCs. HCFCs are synthetic compounds that contain hydrogen, chlorine, fluorine, and carbon. They are known to contribute to ozone depletion, and their phase-out is mandated by international agreements like the Montreal Protocol.</narrative>
  </description>
